# Build & QA Workflow

## Make Targets
Default build/QA via Make targets as defined in [Makefile](mdc:Makefile):
- `make setup` - Full environment setup
- `make fmt` - Format code with Ruff
- `make lint` - Lint with Ruff
- `make test` - Run tests
- `make build` - Build package
- `make publish` - Publish package

## Tool Configuration
- Use Ruff for formatting and linting
- Use uv for venvs, lockfiles, builds, and publishing
- Don't add new tools unless necessary
- If adding tools, wire them through [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml)/Make

## Dependencies
- Don't add new dependencies for trivial tasks
- Prefer standard library or existing stack
- Reference [pyproject.toml](mdc:pyproject.toml) for dependency management